<title>SOUTH AFRICA: AVIS GIVES CAPITALISATION AWARD DETAILS.</title>
<headline>AVIS GIVES CAPITALISATION AWARD DETAILS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African tourism and car rental firm Avis Holdings Ltd said on Thursday 1.52 million shares would be listed on the Johannesburg, Botswana and Namibia bourses on Friday as a result of a capitalisation share award.</p>
<p>Shareholders were given an option of receiving capitalisation shares instead of year dividend of 8.09 cents.</p>
<p>It said the weighted average traded price of the shares on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange for the three day period ended May 29 was 777 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
